# ---- Market data -----------------------------------------------------------
# Paths are ANCHORED with a leading slash. A bare "data/" would match any
# directory of that name at any depth -- including propfirm/data/, which would
# silently drop seven source modules from the repo.
#
# Parquet stores are large and grow without bound (the tick recorder appends
# continuously). Git is the wrong home for them.
#
# WARNING: /data/raw/ticks/ and /data/raw/tick_stream/ are NOT regenerable. Deriv
# serves only the last 24h of tick history, so anything the recorder captured
# beyond that window exists nowhere else. Ignoring them says git is the wrong
# store -- not that they are disposable. They need a real backup.
#
# Candles ARE re-fetchable (365-day rolling window), so losing them is cheap.
/data/*
!/data/.gitkeep
!/data/raw/
/data/raw/*
# The verified symbol registry is small and records what the live API actually
# served rather than what we assumed, so it is worth versioning.
!/data/raw/symbol_registry.json

# ---- Research outputs ------------------------------------------------------
# Sweep results and findings are small and are the point of the project, so they
# stay tracked. Large or regenerable artefacts do not.
*.parquet
*.feather
*.h5
*.pkl

